{title: Standing at the Door}
{subtitle: Revelation 3:20}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 80}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm] | ×8

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I said I'm rich, I've prospered, and I don't need a thing
Not cold and not hot, just a lukewarm offering
But [C]I was poor and blind and naked and I didn't even know
[Gm]And through the rain somebody's knocking, soft and slow
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Look, I am standing at the [Dm]door and knocking
[Eb]If anyone hears my voice [Dm]and opens the door
I [Gm]will come into him and [C]eat with him [Eb]
[Dm]And he with [Gm]me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He said, buy from me gold that's refined by the fire
White garments for your shame and salve for your eyes
[C]Those whom I love I rebuke and discipline
So be [Gm]earnest and repent and let me in
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [Gm] | [C] |
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [C] | [C] |
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [Eb] | [Dm] |
| [Eb] | [Dm] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm]Knock, knock, on a rainy night
[C]I hear your voice
[Eb]Lord, I'm [Dm]opening the door
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Gm]I will come into him, meet with him
[C]Be with him, be [Dm]with [Gm]me
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Gm] |
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [C] | [Eb] [Dm] | ×2
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [Gm] |
